# Live shared service (do not lose this)

This repo is **one website** members use over time, not a batch pipeline and not a laptop-hosted demo.

- **Host:** CloudFront `AppUrl` = SPA + `/api` on one box (`docker/app.Dockerfile`), SQLite on retained EBS. CloudFront is the only HTTP door (VPC origin; port 80 is not world-open). The box may have a public IP for egress (Bedrock, ECR, Google) only. **GitHub → CodeBuild** ships the image. CloudShell is on/off + secrets, not a laptop upload path. Do not split Studio onto static hosting.
- **On / off:** Always-on template = instance running. Off = `ec2 stop-instances` (keep volume). Mail jobs only run when On. Do not use Lambda+API Gateway for the app (Find exceeds 29s). Do not use Aurora 24/7 as the default DB (more expensive than this box).
- **Shared state:** one SQLite file is the club warehouse. Writes on AppUrl are visible to other members. Browser `localStorage` is not shared truth.
- **On-demand:** Home, Week, Studio, Send, Pipeline, Find, Stats are doors. Any order. Studio generate must work against existing contacts (or upsert quick-compose). Do not require Find → comb → Studio → Gmail.
- **Live catalog:** `contacts`, `campaigns` + `campaign_contacts`. Pipeline/Studio/Stats are views. Company = group by domain/name. Staging Find/Week promote via import/Keep.
- **Mail campaign is the registered campaign.** `outreach_campaigns` is not a parallel send ledger.
- **Hosted AI:** `LLM_PROVIDER=bedrock` via `llm.py`. Rank = Haiku-class JSON; Studio may use the UI model.
- **Instance:** t3.small, `INBOX_VERIFY_MODE=mx`. Gate HTML crawl only. No P9. Andre commits; never Cursor as author.

If a change would make two members see different databases, require a laptop to deploy, or make Studio wait on a week loop, it is the wrong change.
